Track 3: Delroy’s Shackle Over Pigeon River
- Story & Context: By the autumn of 2018, when municipal road crews finally dismantled the rogue solar rigs along the Pigeon River Bridge, Delroy Pless had abandoned his gear and vanished into the timber gaps, leaving behind only a copper padlock clamped to the guardrail. The bridge crew discovered that a piezoelectric contact pickup had been permanently sealed into the expansion joint, catching the deep hum of passing tires and transmitting it as an unintended bass drone across the local FM spectrum. To this day, long-haul truckers crossing the river gorge at twilight swear their dashboards briefly override, playing a soft acoustic waltz through the dashboard speakers. "The road forgot what it was paved to find," repeats the phantom broadcast, turning a forgotten infrastructure protest into highway folklore.
